WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.580
Hey guys, Pete here. This will be my Dark
season 3 family trees video. The

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.389
final season of this Netflix original
series answered most of the questions

00:00:09.389 --> 00:00:13.980
related to the four families at the
center of the knot that is Winden, but

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.940
due to the looping nature of some of the
family relations it's a lot to take in

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.890
and keep track of. In this Dark season 3
video I'll be talking about the family

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.730
connection revelations we got, and that
will contain spoilers that would

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.019
potentially ruin things if you haven't
finished the series. For that reason I

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:35.430
wouldn't recommend watching this video
until you've completed the entire third

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.050
season. I do have a family tree video
that I'll link to up at the top if you

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.940
want to get a refresher of who's who
while you're watching season 3. Alright

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.350
then. We did get some major revelations
in how things are connected with the

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.390
families in Dark and it turns out that
Jonas and Martha are the center of it all.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:58.800
Of course, when I say Martha I'm talking
about the one from the alternate world.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.019
the Martha from seasons 1 &amp; 2 who Jonas
fell in love with only to find out she

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:08.189
was his aunt is dead and makes no
further contributions to the family

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:12.150
trees. For that reason I'm not gonna say
"alt" every time I say her name.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.860
This Martha, the one from the alternate
world, is at the center of everything

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.659
because she conceived a child with Jonas. Since we've all watched the season

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:25.860
I won't retell the story in this video,
but in relation to the families Martha

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.479
saves Jonas from the apocalypse in his
world and brings him to hers. He then

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:34.470
meets a slightly younger version of her
who doesn't know anything about time

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:38.340
travel yet and they end up sleeping
together. She gets pregnant as a result

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.810
and that turns out to be the beginning
of all the family tree insanity. She

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.590
gives birth to a character that we've
been calling "the Trio" due to the fact

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:50.850
that he appears as three characters.
Three versions of the same character at

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.729
different points in his life - a boy, an
adult,

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:57.540
and an old man. This character explains
he was never given a name and is

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.340
referred to as "The Unknown" in the
credits and official show materials. The

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.360
Unknown answers one of the biggest
questions we've had. Agnes Nielsen was

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.770
the farthest point back on the Nielsen
family line and we had no idea who

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.060
fathered her son.
According to the official website the

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:19.370
Unknown conceived Tronte in both worlds
with Agnes. Tronte then is the father of

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:25.340
Ulrich, who is the father of Martha, but
also the grandfather of Jonas. it's an

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:30.650
infinite cycle. a massive knot with the
Unknown at the center. on screen we don't

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.700
see the Unknown and Agnes together, and
we never visit the time when she was

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.900
pregnant with Tronte. The explanation
just says that he was conceived in both

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.459
worlds by the same parents. another big
question we had about Agnes and her

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:48.500
brother Noah was who their parents were.
season 3 gives us that answer and it

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.360
turns out to be Silja and Bartosz
Tiedemann. Bartosz of course was Jonas's

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.829
highschool friend that was saved by
stranger Jonas at the end of season 2. he

00:02:57.829 --> 00:03:02.390
ended up in 1888 and was eventually
killed by younger Noah, who turned out to

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:08.780
be his son, in 1921. Silja was taken care
of by Elisabeth Doppler in the future

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:14.540
until she was sent back to 1890 and meets
Bartosz. they become a couple and have Noah

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.230
and Agnes together with Silja dying
while giving birth to their daughter.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:22.639
this is a good time to discuss the
differences in how the family tree plays

00:03:22.639 --> 00:03:27.410
out in Adam's and Eva's worlds. in the
official family tree we can see that

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.310
many of the relationships still exist
but we don't get to see how they played

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.859
out in Eva's world. Silja and Bartosz are
still Agnes parents but we never

00:03:36.859 --> 00:03:41.120
actually meet Silja in her world. Bartosz follows a much different path

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.470
through time, but as far as the family
trees are concerned we end up in the

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:49.940
same place. Silja's parentage is another
example of this. we learned that her

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:55.519
parents are Hannah and Egon in Adam's
world. she traveled back to 1954 and met

00:03:55.519 --> 00:04:00.049
him there. they have an affair in that
time period and she gives birth to Silja

00:04:00.049 --> 00:04:05.180
after leaving him. eventually she travels
back in time where Jonas / Adam kills

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.889
her and he sends Silja to the future
where she grows up until we first meet

00:04:09.889 --> 00:04:16.729
her in 2052. In Ava's world it isn't
clear when this happens since Hannah is

00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:22.669
married to Ulrich in the 2019 timeline
and Egon is a travelling member of

00:04:22.669 --> 00:04:26.789
Eva's group Erit Lux.
the only time we see them together is

00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:30.960
when Egon rescues her from the
apocalypse in that world. at that time

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.180
Hannah was pregnant with Ulrich's child
but she suffers a miscarriage right as

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:40.979
Egon is arriving. Egon and his first
wife Doris are the parents of Claudia

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:45.449
Tiedemann. Claudia is the mother of
Regina who gets cancer in both worlds,

00:04:45.449 --> 00:04:48.330
but we never knew for sure who her
father was.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.990
Tronte was the most likely candidate
because we knew that they had a

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.759
relationship, but it turns out that Bernd
Doppler was Regina's father all along.

00:04:56.759 --> 00:05:00.690
this felt someone out of the blue since
there were no hints to an intimate

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.889
relationship, but it turns out to be
important since it means that Regina is

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:10.349
not a direct descendant of the Jonas and
Martha's line. Regina's husband Aleksander

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:14.819
has a mysterious backstory that fans
have long theorized about. he was born

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:17.909
Boris Niewald
and arrived in Winden with a gunshot

00:05:17.909 --> 00:05:22.530
wound carrying the pistol that will
travel through time and later be used by

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:27.240
Adam to kill Martha from his world. he
used that to run off teen Katharina and

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:32.039
Ulrich who were threatening Regina and
the two form a relationship that sees

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:36.780
them get married and give birth to
Bartosz. his entrance into the story led

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.340
to many theories about him being a time
traveler or at least manipulated by one,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.599
but in the end it turns out he was a guy
on the run. in Eva's world he tells his

00:05:45.599 --> 00:05:49.800
son that he killed a man in Marburg, but
it was an accident. he played a role in

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.759
the apocalypse in both worlds as
director of the power plant, but he was

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:57.919
just a criminal who went straight after
fleeing to Winden and meeting his wife.

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:02.520
speaking of the power plant, Bernd
Doppler's wife Greta expressed doubt

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.630
about him being Helge's real father. in
a conversation with Noah she says the

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:10.259
boy was not born out of love
leading to speculation that she may

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:14.310
have been raped. we don't get a full
explanation of the story here but the

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.090
family tree does give us a name and
confirms that Bernd is not Helga's

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:22.560
father. the name is Anatol Veliev but
there's no information about this

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.479
character. Helge's son Peter has also
been the source of many theories because

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:32.729
we only had a vague backstory of him
arriving in Winden in 1987. season 3

00:06:32.729 --> 00:06:36.990
explained that Helge is his father but
he didn't know about him until

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:41.130
shortly before his mother died. his
mother's name was Ulla Schmidt but we

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:45.840
don't have any other details about her
life or relationship with Helge. in the

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.860
end like Boris Niewald Peter's story
turned out to be just what it looked

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.880
like on the surface. of course he does
get together with Charlotte in both

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.590
worlds and pitches in on the bootstrap
paradox relationship between his wife

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:02.580
and daughter. that they are each other's
mothers was one of the big reveals in

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.050
season 2 and I find it funny looking at
the new family tree since it's not even

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:12.410
really emphasized. now that we know the
origin theirs is just one loop out of many.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:17.370
Charlotte's adopted grandfather HG Tannhaus is a character we learned a lot

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:21.630
about in the final season. we learned
that his great-grandfather Heinrich was

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.560
the founder of Sic Mundus and the origin
of the gold pocket watch.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:29.700
Heinrich initially gave the watch as a
gift to his wife Charlotte who later

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:34.680
died. he started Sic Mundus to learn how
to time travel in order to try to bring

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.510
her back from the dead. he passes the
watch on to his son Gustav who we meet.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:44.880
he's the blind man who owns the factory
where stranger Jonas is working on the

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.470
time machine. he was killed by the
Unknown as he was on his way to tell the

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.670
world about the Time Traveler's he met - 
stranger Jonas and Martha. the Unknown

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:56.820
takes the watch from him and it starts
its journey through time.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:02.400
Gustav Tannhaus' grandson HG is the
clock maker we met in the first two

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.750
seasons, and he turns out to be the
catalyst for everything in a third

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:11.070
"origin" world. I discussed all of this in
my ending explained video and will

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:15.570
probably revisit it in future videos, but
in relation to the family trees the

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:19.740
website does have an easter egg. if you
scroll all the way through Jonas or

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:25.140
Martha's pages the origin worlds family
tree will appear. by default you just see

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:29.640
mirrored versions of the family tree for
Adam and Eva's worlds. we learned in the

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:34.350
closing scene of the series that some of
the characters from the origin world are

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:38.670
the same, but none of the characters that
are direct descendants of Jonas and

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:45.270
Martha through the Unknown exist. this
origin world family tree shows Claudia

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:50.100
and Bernd are married in this world
making Regina's last name Doppler. we get

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:53.190
confirmation that Hannah and Torben are married making

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:57.959
her last name Woller. we can see that in
a world without Charlotte Peter winds up

00:08:57.959 --> 00:09:02.430
with Bernadette Woller and that even
though Boris Niewald exists it doesn't

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.480
look like he ever gets together with
Regina. there's other characters that we

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:11.399
never saw on-screen, these characters
parents that are in the family tree but

00:09:11.399 --> 00:09:15.540
there isn't any additional information
about their lives in the origin world. we

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:20.220
do see Katharina here her last name is
still Albers and that was one other

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.980
reveal that we got in the third season
that her parents were Hermann and Helene

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:31.410
Albers. of course we saw her mother kill
her, she was the nurse at the psychiatric

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:37.079
unit where Ulrich was living out his
years. Hermann Albers was the man that

00:09:37.079 --> 00:09:42.149
Egon talked to when the sheep died back
in season one, and that pretty much wraps

00:09:42.149 --> 00:09:47.160
things up. as mentioned the biggest
reveal is that all of this starts and

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:52.680
essentially ends with Jonas and Marta. on
a bigger scale it starts with HG Tannhaus

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:56.970
who like his great grandfather is
obsessed with time travel because he

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:00.870
wants to go back and save someone who
died. we see this theme repeated

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:05.130
throughout the different worlds and in a
way it seems quite fitting that Jonas

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:10.290
and Martha who would never have existed
in the origin world are able to complete

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:15.420
this process making for at least a
reality where Tannhaus' family never

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:21.630
dies and he never decides to invent a
time machine. what an absolute mess and

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:25.740
knot. it does feel great to have all the
answers now. there's a couple things

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:31.140
there. some people we don't know. they
never told us who Hannah's mother was or

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:35.940
or Daniel Kahnwald's wife but in the end
they didn't turn out to be important but

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.930
beyond that we did get answers to all
the big questions and with that I think

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.860
I'll leave it there. let me know in the
comments what you think. did you catch

